<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Paris protests: A look at the aftermath</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d0bd94ab398f45f6e3a8d963cac23291fe9f1967dc0e4d4301413fd8d74feec</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T11:51:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-paris-protests-a-look-at-the-aftermath" /><summary type="html">Following yesterday's demonstrations in Paris, where violent clashes erupted between police and protesters, our reporter Antonia Kerrigan returns to place de la République.</summary></entry><entry><title>Atlanta’s iconic tavern marks Georgia’s past with an eye on future as midterms approach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8f9293aec6dd227e4dcec6959ede8051955a0123d2734f9eaddb2116d1f213c</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T11:15:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-atlanta-iconic-tavern-marks-georgia-past-eye-future-midterms-approach-ossoff-collins" /><summary type="html">Since it was established in 1956, Manuel’s Tavern in Atlanta has hosted legendary Democratic leaders while its founder played a key role in the city’s move from a Republican to Democratic stronghold. With the state’s Democratic Senator Jon Ossoff leading the polls in the midterms amid rumours of a future presidential run, the tavern is once more at the heart of the political action.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Out-of-control truck kills 13 at Hindu festival in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf8f6a9b11f3f731c6b53e51ebc2bcbee4c2911160cd111e0cf16035d96653a1</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T11:14:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-out-of-control-truck-kills-13-at-hindu-festival-in-india" /><summary type="html">A speeding truck in India killed 13 people when it ploughed into a crowd at a Hindu festival, officials said on Sunday, with President Droupadi Murmu describing the deaths as "heartbreaking".</summary></entry><entry><title>Riots in Tirana enter a fifth day as Albania's anti-government protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ac4e20f0771e829279129c92afbed023ca18342270e5da1052ef5116538af52</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T11:06:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-riots-in-tirana-enter-a-fifth-day-as-albania-s-anti-government-protests-escalate" /><summary type="html">Clashes broke out near the Albanian prime minister’s office in the capital, Tirana, on Saturday as anti-government riots entered a fifth day.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Protests "brought the entire population together for a common purpose"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18eb65adf3f82986083241e9a37d74c6949dae6627da5ffbea43b72fe873565f</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T09:05:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-protests-brought-the-entire-population-together-for-a-common-purpose" /><summary type="html">This weekend, in cities across France, some 800,000 protesters, including students, railway workers and members of the Yellow Vest movement, took to the streets in largely peaceful nationwide demonstrations. Sparked by a month of high school student protests over educational inequality and crumbling school facilities, the movement has grown into a broader outcry over the cost of living, public spending and climate inaction, as people across France say they have reached their breaking point.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Who took part in Saturday's protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61010c0df6c82645becee90e178a8fdbcd15c6fbfed85111528ee9299c09af05</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T09:03:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-who-took-part-in-saturday-s-protests" /><summary type="html">Weeks of student protests over poor conditions in schools and rising anger over the cost of living fuelled calls for a nationwide demonstration on October 17, bringing together youth activists and supporters of the Yellow Vest movement.
 
The main grievance was the cost of living. The protesters demonstrating against it 'didn't get what they wanted', analyses France 24's Shirli Sitbon.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Who was behind the violence at Saturday's protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd91860a3bb313e1bdfbbaf13d0292286071cb1d33f35846d0c27e9d6990a1ef</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T09:01:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-who-was-behind-the-violence-at-saturday-s-protests" /><summary type="html">Violent clashes, fires, vandalism and looting marred demonstrations across France on Saturday as hundreds of thousands of people marched against the rising cost of living and poor conditions in schools. The French Interior Ministry said about 400 people were arrested nationwide. Our partner TV station France 2 examined who was involved in the violence during Saturday's protests.</summary></entry><entry><title>France protests: Did the government make the wrong decisions?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfa7606379560db5f8b20e0c50b424a28deebbc11f42d0d32473f70a8844b2a6</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T09:00:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-protests-did-the-government-make-the-wrong-decisions" /><summary type="html">Police in Paris said Sunday they had arrested a "record" 855 people over protest-related violence in the capital the day before, with the prosecutor's office saying more than 500 were being held in custody. France 24's Shirli Sitbon analyses.</summary></entry><entry><title>PSG back on top of Ligue 1 after stunning Strasbourg comeback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ac8713b8fc13b3ee86259b58cff94884c0a6bc3b7037fa07e96f2354a2527d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:48:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261018-ligue-1-psg-back-on-top-of-ligue-1-after-stunning-strasbourg-comeback" /><summary type="html">After trailing Strasbourg for more than 60 minutes, the Parisians called upon their substitutes to turn the game around. Following their spectacular Champions League victory over Manchester City and ahead of their clash with FC Barcelona, PSG are brimming with confidence.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 A demonstrator died from 'cardiorespiratory arrest' during Paris protests, police say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91709341f78629e730adc76d537ae1e4b530a6e0d18a37c91585c68b00a6a925</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T08:06:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france--a2aec9eab7bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france" /></entry><entry><title>Months-long Indonesia wildfires spew toxic haze across Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f0d012be7e2a21a2afd4d87417964424845dc3c527a15a8f26d0496b98791a8</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T06:30:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-months-long-indonesia-wildfires-spew-toxic-haze-across-southeast-asia" /><summary type="html">Parts of southern Southeast Asia have been put under the highest-level haze alert as wildfires that have swept Indonesia for months continue to belch toxic smoke across the region. The seasonal wildfires are worse this year due to the drought conditions caused by a severe "super-El Nino" effect.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India's 'cockroach' movement founder released from police custody</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fdafc93384ef4dbfeb72c3181c88d53f03d9e91298311b9bb5437a918dbe63d</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T05:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-india-s-cockroach-movement-founder-released-from-police-custody" /><summary type="html">Indian police released Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke from detention on Saturday after the activist was detained ahead of a rally calling for the resignation of India's chief election commissioner. Two other CJP leaders remain in custody after having been arrested while demonstrating at a protest site that police had ruled off-limits.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Around 1,500 shops and retailers damaged during French protests, trade group says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:293a4cb983ef3749cd81ad5b4124a0a7cab34f25e130bea134b3032220eada05</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T03:09:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france--a2aec9eab7bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france" /><summary type="html">Roughly 1,500 shops and retailers were damaged during the demonstrations that swept France on the weekend, many of them looted, the head of the Retail and Trade Federation said Sunday. Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez said that police had arrested more than 1,800 people as outbursts of arson and looting broke out on the margins of peaceful marches. Follow out liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio says Trump to 'analyze' global impact of Russia sanctions during pause</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a516b5cc5485763ef5e0ee9e8d15d6f484e82bd9a2e20754f0b03e4665230a2</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T02:39:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-rubio-says-trump-russia-sanctions-waiver-designed-to-analyze-global-impact--05ec5cb4d55f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-rubio-says-trump-russia-sanctions-waiver-designed-to-analyze-global-impact" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Saturday that US President Donald Trump’s decision to waive sanctions and tariffs on Russia would last 60 days, as the move drew bipartisan criticism and raised fears in Ukraine that Washington could ease further restrictions on Moscow.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>‘Standing up for democracy’: Atlanta ‘No Kings’ rally draws Trump critics ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f13db38ff0c2e6e8c69a615387147dce1d890f7cb05f294ffa7ca9695c8531</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T01:50:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-standing-up-for-democracy-atlanta-no-kings-rally-draws-trump-critics-ahead-of-us-midterms--d077ded60ac1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-standing-up-for-democracy-atlanta-no-kings-rally-draws-trump-critics-ahead-of-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">“No Kings, Vote Now” was the theme of a rally in Atlanta, one of many organised across the US on Saturday. While many demonstrators denounced US President Donald Trump’s policies, organisers said the rally was aimed at getting out the vote in the November 3 midterm elections and protecting democracy in America.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Looters seize on massive French protests to raid and vandalise shops</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7649146807331a1f022ab38b7df85b9651a4b80d78bfd9325deed5b6d3dc2b0</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T20:15:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-looters-seize-massive-french-protests-raid-vandalise-shops-france--258861db12d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-looters-seize-massive-french-protests-raid-vandalise-shops-france" /><summary type="html">Looters on Saturday seized the opportunity to raid and vandalise a host of shops and businesses across France – from bakeries and supermarkets to tech stores – as hundreds of thousands of people took to the streets to protest higher living costs and other grievances.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Chaotic scenes as organisers of French protests claim 800,000 have taken to streets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19a99da999b0219a45712802a5a160143e46940f92a4d2717737d9408ed4b832</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T17:18:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-live-france-s-yellow-vests-throw-their-weight-behind-mounting-student-protests--6890f07a1b1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-live-france-s-yellow-vests-throw-their-weight-behind-mounting-student-protests" /></entry><entry><title>India: Police crack down on New Delhi protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcc63975bb3734fc0157445bca1d18f333f59d52c182b277541cb032ad01b358</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T16:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-india-police-crack-down-on-new-delhi-protests--1c931afbdd20.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-india-police-crack-down-on-new-delhi-protests" /><summary type="html">Student activist Neha Bora, a prominent face of the protests, ‌who was detained on Friday as she tried to reach central Delhi with dozens of supporters, was released on Saturday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Amazon deforestation at 40-year low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab20c7c7c0a7c8b3ea82e909d8b733f14356369debf2bc30237ece7f5dddea69</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T16:07:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-brazil-amazon-deforestation-at-40-year-low--4d1fefdb83e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-brazil-amazon-deforestation-at-40-year-low" /><summary type="html">In Brazil, deforestation in the Amazon has reached its lowest level in 40 years. President Lula is bolstering his environmental record just over a week before the second round of the presidential election, in which he faces Flávio Bolsonaro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine war: "Mothers of Kherson" opera opens in Poland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abeeaf69b9ec540a23f999b6c19c8960048133821dca9c671eb96f6cd3a0d81f</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:57:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-ukraine-war-mothers-of-kherson-opera-opens-in-poland--ba2f9468fd1a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-ukraine-war-mothers-of-kherson-opera-opens-in-poland" /><summary type="html">"Mothers of Kherson" has opened at Poland's National Opera. The performance was co-produced with New York's Metropolitan Opera and created in close association with Save Ukraine, a group helping to bring back Ukrainian children who remain in Russia. More than four years after Russia's invasion of Ukraine, the opera aims to "reawaken" global interest in the war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Protests in France: "Two fires broke out in Place de la République"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc0bbefed5933bf75ef837990bcbbfbd87e46f0f16d7e62323949ab997a0eeda</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:53:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-protests-in-france-two-fires-broke-out-in-place-de-la-r_publique--bd094c565d7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-protests-in-france-two-fires-broke-out-in-place-de-la-r%C3%A9publique" /><summary type="html">Police and protesters clashed in Paris and other French cities on Saturday, with smoke from fires and tear gas filling the air at demonstrations nationwide against high prices, ahead of elections to replace President Emmanuel Macron. "Two fires broke out in Place de la République," reports France 24's Antonia Kerrigan from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Protester’s hand blown off by police grenade as unions say half a million march across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:adf42f149a03f56a004c13d985283aec4ef436b45766c8421bc637d7bf2190ca</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:25:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-live-france-s-yellow-vests-throw-their-weight-behind-mounting-student-protests--6890f07a1b1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-live-france-s-yellow-vests-throw-their-weight-behind-mounting-student-protests" /></entry><entry><title>US: Four killed in Oregon school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a901bd5d40b848c2f8e836364498e73154888de435e00f0dbb0adfebc09a836</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:16:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-us-four-killed-in-oregon-school-shooting--975e94561c5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-us-four-killed-in-oregon-school-shooting" /><summary type="html">The teenage gunman who shot dead three children and a teacher in an Oregon school was a former special needs student there, officials said Friday, as they praised the heroism of people who helped to shorten the rampage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Protests in France: "Living conditions are too harsh"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af2f08b62e0d6bfc21adb471b419a33dc8d733696df9c187d32621016ea652f6</id><updated>2026-10-18T12:40:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:10:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-protests-in-france-living-conditions-are-too-harsh--c10a1f8ea0d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-protests-in-france-living-conditions-are-too-harsh" /><summary type="html">Saturday’s mobilisation in France follows calls on social media to revive the Yellow Vests movement, which emerged in 2018 against social injustice. Student groups protesting since mid-September have urged supporters to join. We discuss this with our journalist on the ground, Antonia Kerrigan, and our guest, Paul Smith, head of Modern Languages at the University of Nottingham.</summary></entry></feed>
